### 1. Enable the Amount Field
To allow users to type the amount without selecting the currency first, remove the disabled={!row.currency} property from the Amount TextField.
**Update your Amount Grid item to this:**
```javascript
<Grid item size={{ xl: 2, lg: 2.8 }}>
  <TextField
    label="Amount *" type="text" value={row.amount} InputLabelProps={{ shrink: true }}
    fullWidth placeholder="0.0000" inputProps={{ style: { textAlign: "right" } }}
    onChange={(e) => {
      const rawVal = e.target.value;
      if (/[^0-9.]/.test(rawVal)) {
        showSnackBar("Only numbers and decimal point are allowed.", "warning"); return;
      }
      if (rawVal === "" || amountRegex.test(rawVal)) { handleRowChange(row.id, "amount", rawVal); }
      else { showSnackBar("Exceeded maximum digits or decimal places.", "warning"); }
    }}
  />
  <Typography variant="caption" sx={{ fontSize: "0.65rem", color: "text.secondary", mt: 0.5, ml: 1.2, display: "block", textAlign: "left" }}>
    Max 16 digits, 4 decimals
  </Typography>
</Grid>

```
### 2. Fix Branch Text Visibility
To prevent the Branch text from being cut off awkwardly without increasing the grid size, apply CSS text truncation (textOverflow: 'ellipsis') directly to the inner input element.
**Update the renderInput inside your Branch Autocomplete to this:**
```javascript
renderInput={(params) => (
  <Tooltip title="Search by Branch Code" placement="top-start">
    <TextField 
      {...params} 
      label="Branch *" 
      placeholder="Enter branch code..." 
      InputLabelProps={{ shrink: true }} 
      inputProps={{
        ...params.inputProps,
        style: { textOverflow: 'ellipsis', whiteSpace: 'nowrap', overflow: 'hidden' }
      }}
      InputProps={{ 
        ...params.InputProps, 
        endAdornment: (
          <Box>
            {branchSearch.loadingId === row.id ? (<CircularProgress color="inherit" size={20} />) : null}
            {params.InputProps.endAdornment}
          </Box>
        ) 
      }} 
    />
  </Tooltip>
)}

```
### 3. Force Currency Dropdown to Always Open Downwards
Material UI flips the dropdown upward when it thinks there isn't enough screen space below. You can force it to always open downwards by adjusting MenuProps, reducing the maximum height slightly, and setting marginThreshold to 0.
**Update your Currency TextField's SelectProps to this:**
```javascript
SelectProps={{ 
  displayEmpty: true, 
  renderValue: (selected) => !selected ? <span style={{ color: 'gray', opacity: 0.8 }}>Select Currency</span> : selected, 
  MenuProps: { 
    anchorOrigin: { vertical: "bottom", horizontal: "left" }, 
    transformOrigin: { vertical: "top", horizontal: "left" }, 
    marginThreshold: 0,
    PaperProps: { style: { maxHeight: 180 } } 
  } 
}}

```
