### 5. Show Exact Backend Error Message
Your previous catch block was prepending "Failed to initiate request: " to the error, which masks the exact backend response. Let's extract the raw backend message directly.
**Update the catch block in your handleSubmit function:**
```javascript
    } catch (error) {
      // Prioritize the exact message/error returned by the backend API
      const errMsg = 
        error?.response?.data?.message || 
        error?.response?.data?.error || 
        error?.message || 
        "System error occurred.";
        
      // Show the raw error directly
